{"availability":"available","full":"dcarpintero/wikisearch","name":"wikisearch","description":"Multilingual Semantic Search with Reranking on a prepared large vectorized dataset comprising 10 million Wikipedia documents. It supports dense retrieval, keyword search, and hybrid search.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":15,"forks":1,"created":"2023-09-27T13:34:28Z","updated":"2023-11-07T10:19:30Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://wikisearch.streamlit.app/","topics":["cohere","cohere-rerank","dense-retrieval","embedding-vectors","generative-ai","large-language-models","python","reranking","semantic-search","streamlit","weaviate","wikipedia"],"demo":"https://wikisearch.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:16.710Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:16.710Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:16.710Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:07:16.710Z","stars":15,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Streamlit App for Multilingual Semantic Search on over 10 million Wikipedia documents vectorized in embeddings by Weaviate. This implementation is based on Cohere´s blog ´Using LLMs for Search´ and its corresponding notebook. It enables to compare the performance of keyword search, dense retrieval and hybrid search to query the Wikipedia dataset. It further demonstrates the use of Cohere Rerank to improve the accuracy of results, and Cohere Generate to provide a reponse based on said ranked results.","Semantic search refers to search algorithms that consider the intent and contextual meaning of search phrases when generating results, rather than solely focusing on keyword matching. It provides more accurate and relevant results by understanding the semantics, or meaning, behind the query.","An embedding is a vector (list) of floating point numbers representing data such as words, sentences, documents, images or audio. Said numerical representation captures the context, hierarchy and similarity of the data. They can be used for downstream tasks such as classification, clustering, outlier detection and semantic search."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dcarpintero/wikisearch/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5a6514e4fbba0bc8bfcb0aa2baa0c674e197b70d39ee39d9ffd2bc583da580f7","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:16.852Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:16.852Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Streamlit App for Multilingual Semantic Search on over 10 million Wikipedia documents vectorized in embeddings by Weaviate. This implementation is based on Cohere´s blog ´Using LLMs for Search´ and its corresponding notebook. It enables to compare the performance of keyword search, dense retrieval and hybrid search to query the Wikipedia dataset. It further demonstrates the use of Cohere Rerank to improve the accuracy of results, and Cohere Generate to provide a reponse based on said ranked results.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dcarpintero/wikisearch/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"5a6514e4fbba0bc8bfcb0aa2baa0c674e197b70d39ee39d9ffd2bc583da580f7","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dcarpintero/wikisearch/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:16.853Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-11-07T10:19:30Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dcarpintero/wikisearch/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:16.853Z","hash":"5a6514e4fbba0bc8bfcb0aa2baa0c674e197b70d39ee39d9ffd2bc583da580f7","originalBytes":10036,"storedBytes":10036,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["search","top","query","lang","list","articles","results","stop","wait","hybrid","where","cohere","default","documents","model","wikipedia","based","optional","query.","response","semantic","str","embeddings","filter","keyword","max","python","retrieval","using","vector","venv","after","answer","attempt","bm25","context","def","d